          "type": "turn",
          "question": "Which chapter holds high blood pressure, and what does that chapter deliberately exclude?",
          "answer": "Diagnosed high blood pressure, or essential hypertension (I10), is found in Chapter 9 of the ICD-10-CM, which covers diseases of the circulatory system. This chapter explicitly excludes:\n\n*   Circulatory disorders that complicate pregnancy or childbirth, which are classified in the obstetric chapter.\n*   Giant cell arteritis and systemic vasculitides, which are found with connective-tissue disorders in the musculoskeletal chapter.\n*   Symptoms like chest pain, palpitations, an abnormal cardiac finding, or a raised blood pressure reading without a confirmed diagnosis. These remain in Chapter 18, \"Symptoms, signs and abnormal findings\" (R00-R99), until a diagnosis is made.\n\n(Sources: `coding-hypertension-i10`, `coding-icd10-chapter-09-circulatory`)\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
